# Console mutation → view sync (required)

Principle: **read-your-writes** — after a successful write (POST/PATCH/DELETE), any on-screen list, tree, or detail that depends on that data must update without requiring a full browser reload.

## Rules

1. **One source of truth per surface** — e.g. site tree state lives in `useContentTree` / `ContentTreeProvider`; child routes (`ContentEditPage`) must call `useContentTreeContext().reload()` (or shared invalidation), not keep a stale sibling copy.
2. **After every successful mutation** that affects visible data: **invalidate cache** (if any) and **refetch or apply an optimistic patch** to all affected views on the current screen.
3. **Prefer pessimistic refetch** unless the patch is trivial and local; optimistic updates must reconcile on API error.
4. **Navigation alone is not sync** — `navigate()` without reloading shared state leaves split layouts (tree + editor) stale.
5. **Logout / site switch** — clear client caches scoped by site/workspace (`contentTreeCache.ts`, `mediaAssetsCache.ts` via `invalidateSiteContentViews()`).

## Checklist for new console features

- [ ] Identified all UI regions that show the mutated entity or its parent list
- [ ] Mutation handler awaits sync (reload / invalidate / local state update)
- [ ] No duplicate hook instances holding the same server-derived list
- [ ] Golden path or UI-relevant test updated when `/console/` list/tree behavior changes

